        "original_id": "d3f39c9e-4da3-56c7-8f0d-dff64229e65a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Cornell, Sully Erna, Tony Rombola, Robbie Merrill, Shannon Larkin\n- Bands: Godsmack\n- Songs: \"Burden in My Hand\"\n- Albums: Down on the Upside\n- Places: Lawrence, Massachusetts\n\nFacts:\n- Chris Cornell, born Christopher John Boyle, was an American musician, singer, and songwriter who was born on July 20, 1964, and died on May 18, 2017.\n- Godsmack is an American rock band from Lawrence, Massachusetts, that was formed in 1995.\n- \"Burden in My Hand,\" written by Chris Cornell, was released on September 18, 1996, as the second single from the 1996 album Down on the Upside.\n- Godsmack is composed of founder, frontman, and songwriter Sully Erna, guitarist Tony Rombola, bassist Robbie Merrill, and drummer Shannon Larkin.",
